WEBVTT

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.336
Higher.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.431
Lieutenant, we're already
at 200,000 meters.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.136
You could thermalize
at this altitude.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.769
I said higher.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.944
We're at 300,000 meters.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.488
Level us off.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.750
Computer, disengage
safety protocols.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.223
Warning.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:30.524
Disengaging safety protocols
presents extreme risk of injury.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:31.962
Override.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:32.963
Acknowledged.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.796
Safety protocols
have been disengaged.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.433
Drop the force field on my mark.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.736
Aye.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.008
Mark.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.551
Bridge to Torres.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.921
I don't believe it.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.426
Report to Engineering
on the double.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.754
Computer, end program.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.111
I was not aware
that protective attire

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.848
was required for this mission.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:32.221
I was on the holodeck...
orbital skydiving.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.817
Leaping from a spacecraft
at exospheric altitudes.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.259
A curious form of recreation.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.796
The probe is ready for launch.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.559
However, there is
still a problem

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.894
with the telemetry link.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.161
Lieutenant?

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.497
Is something wrong?

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.970
Actually, I'm not
feeling so well.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.802
Can you handle the launch
without me?

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.070
You are putting me in charge?

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.406
Problem?

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.504
No. Just unexpected.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.640
Shall I inform the Doctor
you are ill?

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:57.808
No.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.351
Don't.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.508
Captain, someone's
locked on to our probe

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:04.838
with a tractor beam.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.902
It looks like a Malon freighter.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.480
I had a feeling we hadn't
seen the last of them.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.709
Open a channel.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:11.875
Aye, Captain.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:14.317
Starship Voyager
to the Malon vessel.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.014
That probe belongs to us.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.556
Release it immediately.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.055
No response.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.652
Tom, how fast can
you get us there?

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.027
Two hours at least.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.725
They'll be long gone.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.666
If we instruct the probe
to emit a polaron burst,

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.761
it could disrupt
the tractor beam.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.998
Do it.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.373
The beam has been disabled.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.106
Harry, redirect
the probe's course.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.910
The Malon are in pursuit.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.917
That probe can't outrun them.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.577
No.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.849
But we might be able
to hide it from them.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.946
Captain?

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:54.322
The probe surveyed a class-6
gas giant this morning.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.363
I think we should send it
back for a closer look.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:01.264
You're going to steer the probe
into a gas giant.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.631
Captain...

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.602
the atmospheric pressure
will crush it.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:07.196
Not if the Borg shielding
does its job.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.644
Hail them again.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.581
No response.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.279
Voyager to Malon vessel.
Break off your pursuit.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.720
The probe is entering
the giant's upper atmosphere

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.452
and the Malon vessel
is following it in.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.770
The probe's stuck
in a deep layer

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.636
of liquid hydrogen and methane
about 10,000 kilometers below

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.198
the outer atmosphere.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.642
It's not responding to commands.

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:46.804
Any good news?

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:47.937
It's still intact.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.174
It can be repaired.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.079
If we can get it out of there.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.583
Sorry I'm late.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.048
We were just discussing
how to retrieve the probe.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.648
Is there any possibility
of transporting it out?

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.489
No.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.051
Just...

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.323
no.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:08.163
I don't see how we could
get close enough.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.202
Is there any way
to boost transporter range?

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.533
Not in that kind of atmosphere.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:15.267
Well, if we can't
transport it out,

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:18.367
we'll just have
to fly in and grab it.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.912
Perhaps you weren't
paying attention

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.312
when the Malon freighter
imploded.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:26.750
We won't be going
in a Malon freighter, Tuvok.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.652
We'll be going
in our new shuttlecraft.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.622
Oh, here we go again.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:32.919
Let's face it... class-2 shuttles

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.924
just don't cut it
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:38.292
We've needed something bigger
and better since we got here.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.854
It's time we built it.

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.924
Tom, we've been through this
I don't know how many times.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.867
We all appreciate
your enthusiasm...

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.029
Speak for yourself, Commander.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.902
Bottom line...
we don't have time

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:50.568
to design and build
a ship from scratch.

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.168
I knew you were going
to say that.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:55.510
So I've given us a head start.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.843
Behold the Delta Flyer.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:05.050
Ultra-aerodynamic contours,
retractable nacelles,

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:07.558
parametallic hull plating,

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:11.358
unimatrix shielding based on
Tuvok's brilliant design

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:13.763
for the multispatial probe

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:15.858
and a Borg-inspired
weapon system.

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.705
The basic design elements are...

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.364
adequate.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.773
High praise.

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:27.677
If we used isomagnetic EPS
conduits in the plasma manifold,

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:30.443
we could maximize
the power distribution.

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:32.245
That's the spirit, Harry.

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:34.843
My shield designs could be
successfully applied

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.286
to a vessel of this size.

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:37.720
Big of you to admit it, Tuvok.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.087
And you think

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:41.786
it'll be able to withstand
the gas giant's atmosphere.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:42.919
The probe did.

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.190
I'm impressed.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.232
But how quickly can it be built?

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.895
We could replicate the alloys
and the new design components,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.369
use spare parts from storage.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.531
If we worked around the clock,

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.370
we could have it up
and running inside a week.

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:59.206
I'm willing to put in
as much overtime as it takes.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:02.736
I will forgo regeneration
for the duration of the project.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:04.976
What about you, B'Elanna?

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:06.746
Building a new vessel
from scratch...

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:08.878
that's an engineer's dream
come true.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.916
What do you say, Captain?

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:16.888
Why are you all standing around?

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:35.640
Computer, add dynametric
tail fins to the nacelles.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:43.421
Computer, delete
dynametric tail fins.

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:47.454
What'd you do that for?

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.927
We are not designing
a "hot rod," Lieutenant.

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:53.488
That is exactly
what we're designing...

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:58.060
a 24th century, warp-powered,
ultra-responsive hot rod.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:00.367
Your embellishments
are purely decorative.

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.134
They serve no practical purpose.

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:03.334
No, I beg to differ.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.639
If we make this thing
look mean enough,

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:08.077
other ships are going to think
twice before taking us on.

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.808
I suggest we return
our attention

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:12.043
to the matter
of structural integrity.

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:13.517
Agreed.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:16.783
Lieutenant Torres' hull design
is flawed.

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:18.483
We should be using
tetraburnium alloys

00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:20.719
instead of titanium.

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:24.286
Uh, B'Elanna?

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:27.196
Sounds fine to me.

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:32.367
I'm going to finish up
the thruster specs.

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.056
It's open.

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:56.588
Hey.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:58.823
Thruster specs.

00:09:58.898 --> 00:09:59.887
Thanks.

00:09:59.966 --> 00:10:01.661
Where you running off to?

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:03.224
My quarters.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.361
Stay a while.

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:09.738
I'll, uh, replicate some dinner,
a bottle of burgundy.

00:10:09.809 --> 00:10:12.937
We deserve a break,
don't you think?

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:15.071
Not tonight.

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:17.047
B'Elanna...

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:19.346
what's going on?

00:10:19.418 --> 00:10:21.249
Nothing.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.754
Well, then
how come it's impossible

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:26.087
to have a conversation with you?

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:28.688
I'm sorry.

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:30.058
I don't want an apology.

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:31.357
I want an explanation.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.127
Tom, I'm tired.

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:37.965
Asleep is more like it.

00:10:38.104 --> 00:10:42.097
You hardly said three words
in that last meeting.

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:44.574
And then when Seven
changed your design,

00:10:44.644 --> 00:10:46.111
you acted like...

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:48.078
like you didn't care.

00:10:48.147 --> 00:10:50.240
I guess I didn't.

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:55.410
I don't get it.

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:59.891
How many times have we talked
about how great it would be

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:02.018
to do what we're doing now?

00:11:02.094 --> 00:11:05.325
To really collaborate...
my piloting skills

00:11:05.398 --> 00:11:07.025
and your engineering expertise.

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:09.567
We finally get the chance
to create something

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:11.398
together from the ground up

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:14.598
and you're not the slightest
bit enthusiastic?

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:16.539
I'm doing my job, aren't I?

00:11:16.609 --> 00:11:19.703
I delivered the thruster
specs on schedule.

00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:22.145
B'Elanna, I'm not your boss.

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:24.876
I'm not questioning
your productivity

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:28.147
or keeping tabs
on how many hours you put in.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.848
I just want to know
what's going on.

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:37.319
I have to go.

00:11:56.315 --> 00:12:01.150
Computer, activate holodeck
program Torres 2-1-6.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.245
The program is active.

00:12:03.322 --> 00:12:05.517
Disengage safety protocols.

00:12:05.591 --> 00:12:08.151
Warning.
Disengaging safety protocols

00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:10.525
presents extreme risk of injury.

00:12:10.596 --> 00:12:12.587
Override.

00:12:12.665 --> 00:12:13.791
Acknowledged.

00:12:13.866 --> 00:12:16.835
Safety protocols
have been disengaged.

00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:01.341
Ooh!

00:13:19.265 --> 00:13:20.823
Ensign, put us
into a high orbit.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.198
I want to stay well-above
that ionospheric turbulence.

00:13:23.269 --> 00:13:24.702
Aye, ma'am.

00:13:25.905 --> 00:13:26.929
There's the probe.

00:13:27.039 --> 00:13:28.939
10,000 kilometers

00:13:29.041 --> 00:13:31.839
beneath all that methane
but still intact.

00:13:31.911 --> 00:13:33.037
We're not alone.

00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:35.603
I'm reading massive
theta radiation.

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:37.615
It's being dumped
by a Malon freighter

00:13:37.683 --> 00:13:40.311
approaching from the far side
of the planet.

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:41.512
They're hailing.

00:13:41.587 --> 00:13:43.452
Well, they're more talkative
than the last ones.

00:13:43.522 --> 00:13:44.454
Open a channel.

00:13:44.523 --> 00:13:45.455
Aye, sir.

00:13:45.524 --> 00:13:47.321
Leave orbit of this planet now.

00:13:47.393 --> 00:13:49.384
I don't believe
we've been introduced.

00:13:49.461 --> 00:13:50.621
I'm Captain Janeway.

00:13:50.696 --> 00:13:52.527
I know exactly who you are.

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:54.156
You are the person responsible

00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:56.565
for the destruction
of one of our freighters

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:59.399
and the deaths
of nine Malon citizens.

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:01.336
I'm very sorry
that lives were lost,

00:14:01.407 --> 00:14:03.739
but you're leaving out
an important detail.

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:06.471
Your people were trying
to steal a probe from us.

00:14:06.545 --> 00:14:09.070
We warned them to stay away
from the gas giant,

00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:10.638
but they didn't listen.

00:14:10.716 --> 00:14:14.152
I'm taking your probe
as compensation for our losses.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.154
That's going to be
a little difficult.

00:14:16.222 --> 00:14:17.849
It's stuck
beneath the atmosphere

00:14:17.923 --> 00:14:20.483
of the same gas giant
that crushed your other ship.

00:14:20.559 --> 00:14:23.221
My people are expert
at salvage operations.

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:25.923
Well, Mr...

00:14:25.998 --> 00:14:28.091
Vrelk. Controller Vrelk.

00:14:28.167 --> 00:14:30.101
Vrelk.

00:14:30.169 --> 00:14:32.933
We have a little expertise
of our own.

00:14:33.005 --> 00:14:34.939
We're a very determined crew.

00:14:35.074 --> 00:14:37.941
So my suggestion is
that you leave orbit

00:14:38.077 --> 00:14:39.908
and in the future,
if you come across anything

00:14:39.979 --> 00:14:42.777
that bears the insignia
of the USS Voyager,

00:14:42.848 --> 00:14:44.816
head in the other direction.

00:14:44.884 --> 00:14:46.613
You are making a serious error.

00:14:46.685 --> 00:14:48.414
End transmission.

00:14:49.955 --> 00:14:53.413
Why would people in the business
of toxic waste disposal

00:14:53.492 --> 00:14:55.790
be so anxious
to get hold of a probe?

00:14:55.861 --> 00:14:57.123
It's not just any probe.

00:14:57.196 --> 00:14:58.788
It's multispatial technology.

00:14:58.864 --> 00:15:01.424
Maybe they think it'll
help them find new places

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.592
to dump their garbage.

00:16:23.015 --> 00:16:24.277
B'Elanna.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.840
What a nice surprise.

00:16:25.918 --> 00:16:28.386
I was just getting
ready to close.

00:16:28.454 --> 00:16:29.716
Business has been slow

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:32.586
with so many people
busy on the new shuttle.

00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:35.388
Oh.

00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:38.828
I-I was just hoping
we could catch up.

00:16:38.897 --> 00:16:40.091
You want to catch up?

00:16:40.165 --> 00:16:41.189
W-with me?

00:16:41.266 --> 00:16:43.393
If you have the time.

00:16:43.469 --> 00:16:44.800
Are you kidding?

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.634
Yeah, we... can I
get you something?

00:16:49.541 --> 00:16:51.839
Name your poison.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.844
Oh.

00:16:55.347 --> 00:16:56.371
Um...

00:16:56.448 --> 00:16:58.109
Come on, B'Elanna,
I handed that one to you

00:16:58.183 --> 00:16:59.172
on a silver platter.

00:16:59.251 --> 00:17:00.946
Huh?

00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:02.178
Name your poison?

00:17:02.254 --> 00:17:04.051
I was expecting one of those

00:17:04.123 --> 00:17:07.251
scathing but affectionate
insults you always make

00:17:07.326 --> 00:17:08.384
about my cooking.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.484
Sorry.

00:17:09.561 --> 00:17:12.121
You'll feel wittier
on a full stomach.

00:17:12.197 --> 00:17:13.721
So, uh, what'll it be?

00:17:13.799 --> 00:17:16.233
You know, actually...

00:17:16.301 --> 00:17:20.067
I was hoping
for banana pancakes.

00:17:20.139 --> 00:17:22.505
Huh. I-I-I don't think
I ever heard

00:17:22.574 --> 00:17:24.405
of banana pancakes before.

00:17:24.476 --> 00:17:28.139
My grandmother used to make them
for me when I was a kid.

00:17:28.213 --> 00:17:30.443
It's always put a smile
on my face.

00:17:30.516 --> 00:17:32.916
Well, then...

00:17:33.018 --> 00:17:35.077
one smile coming right up.

00:17:39.858 --> 00:17:44.022
Computer,
one stack of banana pancakes.

00:17:53.672 --> 00:17:55.071
Smells delicious.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.971
Thanks.

00:18:06.418 --> 00:18:07.715
So how have you been?

00:18:07.786 --> 00:18:10.516
Oh, just great.

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:13.251
My security training
is going really well.

00:18:13.325 --> 00:18:15.623
Tuvok told me the other day
that I'm, uh...

00:18:16.995 --> 00:18:19.225
Not completely inept.

00:18:22.768 --> 00:18:24.235
Aren't you going to try them?

00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:26.294
Oh, sure.

00:18:37.082 --> 00:18:38.140
Well?

00:18:42.254 --> 00:18:43.983
Delicious.

00:18:46.391 --> 00:18:48.825
I have to get back to work.

00:19:01.006 --> 00:19:02.473
What are they still doing here?

00:19:02.541 --> 00:19:04.008
Apparently, they're not willing

00:19:04.076 --> 00:19:05.634
to give up on the probe
so easily.

00:19:05.711 --> 00:19:07.269
The question is:
How do they expect

00:19:07.346 --> 00:19:08.608
to get their hands on it?

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:09.874
It's reasonable to assume

00:19:09.948 --> 00:19:12.109
they're waiting for us
to retrieve the probe,

00:19:12.184 --> 00:19:15.881
at which time, they'll
attempt to steal it again.

00:19:15.954 --> 00:19:18.115
Maybe, but they have to know
we're prepared for that.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.021
If they were planning
to fight, you'd think

00:19:20.092 --> 00:19:22.151
they'd call in reinforcements,
try to outgun us.

00:19:22.227 --> 00:19:26.186
Sensors don't show any other
Malon ships in the area.

00:19:26.265 --> 00:19:27.562
Seven of Nine to the Captain.

00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:28.657
Janeway here.

00:19:28.734 --> 00:19:30.258
Report to the Astrometrics Lab.

00:19:30.335 --> 00:19:33.202
I have important information
regarding the Malon vessel.

00:19:34.606 --> 00:19:35.698
Tuvok?

00:19:40.212 --> 00:19:41.509
What have you got?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.912
I've been using
coherent neutrino beams

00:19:43.982 --> 00:19:46.678
to document activity aboard
the Malon freighter.

00:19:46.752 --> 00:19:49.220
In other words,
you've been spying on them.

00:19:49.288 --> 00:19:51.722
I've made a troubling discovery.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.849
This is a polythermal image

00:19:53.926 --> 00:19:56.019
of an interior section
of the alien ship.

00:19:56.094 --> 00:19:58.392
The shaded figures you see
are Malon crew members.

00:19:58.463 --> 00:20:00.931
That appears to be
a small ship.

00:20:01.033 --> 00:20:04.264
Correct. The Malon
are constructing a spacecraft

00:20:04.336 --> 00:20:06.270
composed of tetraburnium alloys.

00:20:06.338 --> 00:20:09.068
Theoretically, such a ship
would be capable

00:20:09.141 --> 00:20:12.110
of withstanding extreme
atmospheric pressures.

00:20:12.177 --> 00:20:13.701
I'll be damned.

00:20:13.779 --> 00:20:15.940
They're going after
the probe themselves.

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:17.276
That's not all, Captain.

00:20:17.349 --> 00:20:20.409
According to my projections,
they will finish construction

00:20:20.485 --> 00:20:23.511
of their vessel at least 36
hours before we finish ours.

00:20:28.493 --> 00:20:30.290
Well, then...

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:31.454
I'd say we've got

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:33.998
an old-fashioned space race
on our hands.

00:20:41.707 --> 00:20:43.402
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:20:43.475 --> 00:20:45.966
We've stepped up the pace
of construction

00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:49.241
in order to finish our shuttle
before the Malon finish theirs.

00:20:49.314 --> 00:20:51.612
According to Seven's
most recent intelligence,

00:20:51.683 --> 00:20:54.083
we've gained some ground
over the last 24 hours,

00:20:54.152 --> 00:20:57.986
putting us in a virtual dead
heat with our competitors.

00:20:58.056 --> 00:20:59.421
I keep telling you

00:20:59.491 --> 00:21:01.482
we've got to reinforce
the hull with kellinite.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:02.891
That's all there is to it.

00:21:02.961 --> 00:21:05.725
Proposing the same flawed
strategy over and over again

00:21:05.797 --> 00:21:07.321
will not make it
more effective, Ensign.

00:21:07.399 --> 00:21:08.923
Well, we've got
to come up with something

00:21:09.067 --> 00:21:10.898
or we'll never get this thing
off the ground.

00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:18.639
Vorik, turn that damn thing off.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.541
I can't hear myself think.

00:21:20.612 --> 00:21:21.738
Sorry, sir.

00:21:21.813 --> 00:21:24.111
Look, we could spend

00:21:24.182 --> 00:21:27.743
weeks trying to solve this,
but we've got a ticking clock.

00:21:27.819 --> 00:21:30.811
Engines are working;
weapon systems are on line.

00:21:30.889 --> 00:21:33.449
I say we launch now
and hope for the best.

00:21:33.525 --> 00:21:37.154
Mr. Paris, that is perhaps
the most illogical statement

00:21:37.229 --> 00:21:38.321
you've ever made.

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:42.232
Unless we find a way

00:21:42.301 --> 00:21:44.166
to reconfigure
the structural integrity field,

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:47.205
the hull will incur
microfractures during descent.

00:21:47.272 --> 00:21:49.536
Microfractures, Tuvok.

00:21:49.608 --> 00:21:51.633
Doesn't necessarily mean
we'll have a hull breach.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:54.804
And if we do, I suppose
these useless design

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.939
elements from your
"Captain Proton" scenario

00:21:57.015 --> 00:21:58.505
will compensate for the problem.

00:21:58.583 --> 00:22:02.815
Hey, every one of these knobs
and levers is fully functional.

00:22:02.888 --> 00:22:03.912
And completely superfluous.

00:22:04.022 --> 00:22:05.182
Maybe to you.

00:22:05.257 --> 00:22:07.623
I am tired of tapping panels.

00:22:07.693 --> 00:22:09.490
For once, I want controls

00:22:09.561 --> 00:22:12.291
that let me actually feel
the ship I'm piloting.

00:22:12.364 --> 00:22:13.296
Where you going?

00:22:13.365 --> 00:22:14.559
Holodeck.

00:22:14.633 --> 00:22:16.624
What for?

00:22:16.702 --> 00:22:19.728
To find out
if this microfracture problem

00:22:19.805 --> 00:22:21.272
is a fatal flaw.

00:22:27.479 --> 00:22:29.344
Computer,
activate immersion shielding.

00:22:29.414 --> 00:22:32.349
Immersion shielding activated.

00:22:32.417 --> 00:22:34.351
Commence descent sequence.

00:22:34.419 --> 00:22:37.445
Range to probe...
30,000 kilometers. 25,000.

00:22:37.522 --> 00:22:39.319
Warning.

00:22:39.391 --> 00:22:42.588
Atmospheric pressure
is exceeding tolerance levels.

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:44.219
Rapid ascent recommended.

00:22:44.296 --> 00:22:45.354
Continue descent.

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:47.955
Acknowledged. Range to probe...
10,000 kilometers.

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:49.727
Disengage safety protocols.

00:22:49.801 --> 00:22:51.962
Warning.
Disengaging safety protocols

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.970
presents extreme risk of injury.

00:22:54.106 --> 00:22:54.970
Override.

00:22:55.107 --> 00:22:56.233
Acknowledged.

00:22:56.308 --> 00:22:58.799
Safety protocols
have been disengaged.

00:22:58.877 --> 00:23:02.904
Warning. Atmospheric pressure
is exceeding tolerance levels.

00:23:03.014 --> 00:23:05.448
Reroute power
from secondary systems

00:23:05.517 --> 00:23:07.178
to structural integrity.

00:23:07.252 --> 00:23:08.241
Acknowledged.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.517
Microfractures are present
in zones one and four.

00:23:19.798 --> 00:23:22.596
The Malon are venting
a theta radiation cloud.

00:23:22.667 --> 00:23:24.692
Our shields are
down to 89 percent.

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:26.533
Ensign, back us off.

00:23:26.605 --> 00:23:28.072
Vrelk is hailing.

00:23:30.575 --> 00:23:32.304
On screen.

00:23:33.211 --> 00:23:35.145
That was rude, wasn't it?

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:39.809
But we still have quite a bit
of antimatter waste to expel.

00:23:39.885 --> 00:23:42.718
I hope we didn't
damage your shields.

00:23:42.788 --> 00:23:44.153
Our shields are fine.

00:23:44.222 --> 00:23:48.625
Mmm. Well, we only ejected a
small amount of waste this time.

00:23:48.693 --> 00:23:51.890
We still have much, much more
to get rid of.

00:23:51.963 --> 00:23:54.625
Your shields
may not be able to stand

00:23:54.699 --> 00:23:56.963
even higher levels
of theta radiation.

00:23:57.035 --> 00:23:59.560
I've already told you
we're not going anywhere.

00:23:59.638 --> 00:24:01.833
Let's stop playing these games,
Captain.

00:24:01.907 --> 00:24:04.171
You've scanned my ship;
I've scanned yours.

00:24:04.242 --> 00:24:05.504
We each know

00:24:05.577 --> 00:24:08.341
the other is building a vessel
to retrieve the probe.

00:24:08.413 --> 00:24:11.905
What you don't know is that my
vessel will be ready to launch

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:13.347
in less than two days.

00:24:13.418 --> 00:24:14.749
You're too far behind.

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:16.754
Well, if you're so far ahead,

00:24:16.822 --> 00:24:19.188
why bother
trying to scare us away?

00:24:19.257 --> 00:24:23.921
Just trying to save you
the embarrassment of losing.

00:24:25.864 --> 00:24:28.560
You think they're
really two days away?

00:24:28.633 --> 00:24:29.565
He's probably bluffing,

00:24:29.634 --> 00:24:31.033
but we're not going
to take any chances.

00:24:31.102 --> 00:24:32.626
We've got to speed up
construction somehow.

00:24:32.704 --> 00:24:34.729
We'd also better find a way
to shore up our shields

00:24:34.806 --> 00:24:36.603
in case Vrelk decides
to do any more venting.

00:24:36.675 --> 00:24:38.302
Good idea.

00:24:38.376 --> 00:24:40.071
Janeway to Lieutenant Torres.

00:24:41.613 --> 00:24:43.672
Computer, locate
Lieutenant Torres.

00:24:43.748 --> 00:24:46.216
Lieutenant Torres
is in Holodeck 1.

00:24:46.284 --> 00:24:49.219
Get down there.

00:24:49.287 --> 00:24:50.447
Warning.

00:24:50.522 --> 00:24:52.752
Hull microfractures are present

00:24:52.824 --> 00:24:55.190
in zones one, two,
three and four.

00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:56.955
Hull breach is imminent.

00:24:57.028 --> 00:24:58.962
Repeat: Hull microfractures

00:24:59.097 --> 00:25:03.466
are present in zones one,
two, three and four.

00:25:03.535 --> 00:25:05.298
Hull breach is imminent.

00:25:05.370 --> 00:25:07.531
Computer, freeze program.

00:25:11.643 --> 00:25:13.270
B'Elanna.

00:25:13.345 --> 00:25:16.041
Chakotay to Sick Bay.
Medical emergency.

00:25:34.332 --> 00:25:35.765
What am I doing here?

00:25:35.834 --> 00:25:38.359
You had an accident
on the holodeck.

00:25:40.906 --> 00:25:42.339
How long was I out?

00:25:42.407 --> 00:25:44.238
Almost 12 hours.

00:25:49.881 --> 00:25:51.280
I'd better get back to work.

00:25:51.349 --> 00:25:52.316
Not just yet.

00:25:52.384 --> 00:25:53.316
Why?

00:25:53.385 --> 00:25:54.716
The Captain's asked
me to keep you here.

00:25:54.786 --> 00:25:56.185
But I feel fine.

00:25:58.189 --> 00:26:00.248
Would you excuse us,
please, Doctor?

00:26:04.429 --> 00:26:05.521
Captain, what's going on?

00:26:08.934 --> 00:26:11.129
When the Doctor examined you...

00:26:13.438 --> 00:26:16.703
he found evidence
of internal bleeding,

00:26:16.775 --> 00:26:21.872
fractured vertebrae,
contusions, cranial trauma.

00:26:21.947 --> 00:26:23.881
I guess the accident
was pretty serious.

00:26:23.949 --> 00:26:27.180
The injuries I'm talking about
didn't happen recently.

00:26:27.252 --> 00:26:30.779
Some of them are weeks,
even months old.

00:26:30.855 --> 00:26:32.288
Well, I'm an engineer.

00:26:32.357 --> 00:26:34.552
I've had my share
of bumps and bruises.

00:26:34.626 --> 00:26:36.719
But you didn't seek
treatment for any of these.

00:26:36.795 --> 00:26:39.286
I don't run to Sick Bay
every time I stub my toe.

00:26:39.364 --> 00:26:42.265
Some of these injuries were
life-threatening, B'Elanna.

00:26:42.334 --> 00:26:44.598
Do I look like I'm dying?

00:26:46.538 --> 00:26:49.939
The Doctor says many of
the wounds were treated...

00:26:50.041 --> 00:26:52.441
by someone
with the medical expertise

00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:54.501
of a first-year nursing student.

00:26:56.114 --> 00:26:58.412
Oh, that's ridiculous.

00:26:58.483 --> 00:26:59.745
Is it?

00:26:59.818 --> 00:27:02.810
We investigated
today's accident.

00:27:04.756 --> 00:27:06.849
You turned off
the safety protocols

00:27:06.925 --> 00:27:08.586
during the holo-simulation.

00:27:08.660 --> 00:27:09.627
Why?

00:27:09.694 --> 00:27:11.628
We have
a microfracture problem.

00:27:11.696 --> 00:27:15.029
With the safety protocols on,
there's no way to be sure

00:27:15.100 --> 00:27:17.432
what would happen
during a real flight.

00:27:17.502 --> 00:27:20.164
You don't really expect me
to believe that, do you?

00:27:20.238 --> 00:27:22.502
Are you calling me a liar?

00:27:22.574 --> 00:27:25.475
According to the holodeck logs,
you've been spending

00:27:25.543 --> 00:27:28.273
a lot of time there
over the last few months.

00:27:32.484 --> 00:27:34.247
If I were to check...

00:27:36.054 --> 00:27:38.318
would I find
that you've been running

00:27:38.390 --> 00:27:40.858
other programs
without safety protocols?

00:27:40.925 --> 00:27:43.894
Would you like to look
at my personal logs as well?

00:27:43.962 --> 00:27:46.226
B'Elanna, I'm worried about you.

00:27:46.297 --> 00:27:48.697
If there's something wrong,
I want to help.

00:27:48.767 --> 00:27:50.735
Nothing's wrong.

00:27:52.504 --> 00:27:54.062
Okay?

00:27:54.139 --> 00:27:56.130
No. It's not okay.

00:27:56.207 --> 00:27:57.333
And until you decide

00:27:57.409 --> 00:27:59.502
to be more forthcoming,
you'll remain

00:27:59.577 --> 00:28:01.374
under the Doctor's supervision,

00:28:01.446 --> 00:28:03.880
which means
you're off the shuttle project.

00:28:04.015 --> 00:28:04.982
I'm sorry.

00:28:06.351 --> 00:28:07.511
I'm not.

00:28:13.825 --> 00:28:16.055
Now I know
there's something wrong.

00:28:27.272 --> 00:28:30.070
Engines are operating at close
to 90 percent efficiency.

00:28:30.141 --> 00:28:32.541
Seven's got her new
weapon system on line

00:28:32.610 --> 00:28:35.545
and if we can just solve
that microfracture problem,

00:28:35.613 --> 00:28:37.080
we'll be ready to go.

00:28:37.148 --> 00:28:38.080
Keep on it.

00:28:38.149 --> 00:28:39.138
Now...

00:28:41.119 --> 00:28:43.451
let's talk about B'Elanna.

00:28:45.957 --> 00:28:48.653
Tom, you had no idea
about these injuries

00:28:48.727 --> 00:28:50.092
or how she got them?

00:28:51.496 --> 00:28:53.589
She never complained
about being hurt.

00:28:53.665 --> 00:28:56.190
But then again, she's barely
speaking to me lately.

00:28:57.702 --> 00:28:59.499
It's almost as if she's been

00:28:59.571 --> 00:29:01.971
intentionally trying
to hurt herself.

00:29:02.040 --> 00:29:03.439
You think all these injuries

00:29:03.508 --> 00:29:05.203
have been happening
on the holodeck?

00:29:05.276 --> 00:29:06.300
Well, where else?

00:29:06.377 --> 00:29:08.038
If they'd happened
while she was working

00:29:08.113 --> 00:29:11.241
as she claims, somebody would've
filed an injury report.

00:29:11.316 --> 00:29:14.717
Any idea what sort of programs
she's been running?

00:29:17.522 --> 00:29:19.615
You're thinking
the same thing I am.

00:29:21.726 --> 00:29:22.886
I hate to go digging around

00:29:22.994 --> 00:29:24.791
in someone's personal
holodeck programs,

00:29:24.863 --> 00:29:26.421
but if she won't tell us
what's going on

00:29:26.498 --> 00:29:27.829
I don't think
we have much choice.

00:29:27.899 --> 00:29:29.423
Tom, what do you think?

00:29:32.537 --> 00:29:34.095
He's right.

00:29:36.574 --> 00:29:37.973
Start digging.

00:29:59.297 --> 00:30:01.128
I'm sleeping.

00:30:02.734 --> 00:30:04.702
Oh.

00:30:06.738 --> 00:30:07.864
Hi.

00:30:07.939 --> 00:30:09.236
Hi.

00:30:11.843 --> 00:30:14.437
I thought you were the Doctor
making a house call.

00:30:14.512 --> 00:30:17.811
He let you
out of the cell block, huh?

00:30:19.851 --> 00:30:24.686
He thinks familiar surroundings
will help speed my recovery.

00:30:24.756 --> 00:30:26.815
Recovery from what?

00:30:26.891 --> 00:30:28.415
That's what I said.

00:30:28.493 --> 00:30:32.554
He thinks I'm suffering
from clinical depression.

00:30:32.630 --> 00:30:34.564
Are you depressed?

00:30:36.134 --> 00:30:37.692
What are you,

00:30:37.769 --> 00:30:39.964
the new Ship's Counselor?

00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:44.340
No.

00:30:44.409 --> 00:30:45.899
Just a friend.

00:30:45.977 --> 00:30:48.707
This whole thing
is so ridiculous.

00:30:48.780 --> 00:30:51.078
I don't report a few scrapes

00:30:51.149 --> 00:30:55.552
and suddenly Janeway thinks
there's something wrong with me.

00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:57.178
Typical Starfleet, huh?

00:30:57.255 --> 00:30:59.416
You have been running
holodeck programs

00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:01.117
without safety protocols.

00:31:05.230 --> 00:31:06.356
A few.

00:31:06.431 --> 00:31:08.626
But I haven't put
anybody else at risk

00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:10.895
and it's nothing
that I can't handle.

00:31:13.571 --> 00:31:15.061
Tell you what.

00:31:15.139 --> 00:31:17.607
What do you say you and I pay
a little visit to the holodeck?

00:31:17.675 --> 00:31:20.371
You can show me some of the
programs you've been running.

00:31:20.445 --> 00:31:21.377
Right now?

00:31:21.446 --> 00:31:23.539
Sure. Maybe if I see
what you've been up to,

00:31:23.615 --> 00:31:26.516
I can convince the Captain
there's nothing to worry about.

00:31:26.584 --> 00:31:29.280
She's taken away
my holodeck privileges.

00:31:29.354 --> 00:31:31.584
Consider them restored.

00:31:45.637 --> 00:31:49.539
Computer, activate holoprogram
Torres Zeta-1.

00:31:49.607 --> 00:31:50.972
Program activated.

00:31:51.109 --> 00:31:52.269
What are you doing?

00:31:53.344 --> 00:31:54.436
What?

00:32:01.286 --> 00:32:02.776
Computer, freeze program.

00:32:02.854 --> 00:32:04.845
Computer, belay that command!

00:32:09.027 --> 00:32:10.187
Turn it off!

00:32:10.261 --> 00:32:12.092
Not until you tell me
what it is.

00:32:12.163 --> 00:32:13.721
You know what it is!

00:32:20.738 --> 00:32:22.205
Who's this?

00:32:22.273 --> 00:32:24.207
Li Paz.

00:32:24.275 --> 00:32:25.708
Don't you recognize him?

00:32:25.777 --> 00:32:27.335
Oh, I recognize them all.

00:32:27.412 --> 00:32:28.538
Meyer...

00:32:28.613 --> 00:32:29.637
Nelson...

00:32:29.714 --> 00:32:31.306
Sahreen.

00:32:31.382 --> 00:32:32.576
You created a program

00:32:32.650 --> 00:32:35.244
to watch all our Maquis friends
get slaughtered.

00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:36.878
What I want to know is why.

00:32:38.022 --> 00:32:39.512
I thought we came
down here to talk

00:32:39.590 --> 00:32:40.614
about safety protocols.

00:32:40.692 --> 00:32:41.886
This has nothing
to do with that.

00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:43.154
I'm not so sure.

00:32:43.227 --> 00:32:45.923
The logs show you only ran
this program for 47 seconds...

00:32:45.997 --> 00:32:48.465
the day after I gave you
the news about the massacre.

00:32:48.533 --> 00:32:50.626
Then you shut it down
and started running

00:32:50.702 --> 00:32:52.897
the most dangerous programs
you could find

00:32:52.971 --> 00:32:54.302
with the safeties off.

00:32:54.372 --> 00:32:55.304
Why?!

00:32:55.373 --> 00:32:56.635
This is ridiculous.
I'm leaving.

00:32:56.708 --> 00:32:57.970
Computer, seal the doors.

00:32:58.042 --> 00:32:59.202
You can't do this!

00:32:59.277 --> 00:33:00.403
The hell I can't.

00:33:00.478 --> 00:33:03.174
You're not going anywhere until
you tell me what's going on.

00:33:05.683 --> 00:33:07.048
B'Elanna...

00:33:07.118 --> 00:33:10.053
why are you intentionally
trying to hurt yourself?

00:33:12.023 --> 00:33:13.456
I don't know.

00:33:13.524 --> 00:33:15.685
Are you trying
to commit suicide?

00:33:17.028 --> 00:33:17.926
No.

00:33:18.062 --> 00:33:19.290
Then why?

00:33:20.732 --> 00:33:22.427
Because...

00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:27.233
because if I sprain my ankle,
at least I feel something.

00:33:27.305 --> 00:33:29.136
What do you mean?

00:33:29.207 --> 00:33:32.199
I'm not trying to kill myself.

00:33:32.276 --> 00:33:35.939
I'm trying to see
if I'm still alive.

00:33:36.014 --> 00:33:38.005
I don't understand.

00:33:45.623 --> 00:33:47.750
When you look
at those corpses...

00:33:47.825 --> 00:33:49.486
how do you feel?

00:33:52.864 --> 00:33:54.832
Sad.

00:33:54.899 --> 00:33:56.423
Angry.

00:33:56.501 --> 00:34:00.062
Maybe a little guilty that I
wasn't there to die with them.

00:34:00.138 --> 00:34:01.162
Not me.

00:34:01.239 --> 00:34:03.070
I don't feel anything at all.

00:34:03.141 --> 00:34:05.507
B'Elanna, the Maquis
were like our adopted family.

00:34:05.576 --> 00:34:08.511
I can understand you trying to
block out that kind of pain...

00:34:08.579 --> 00:34:11.104
You don't understand.

00:34:11.182 --> 00:34:12.843
It's not just the pain.

00:34:12.917 --> 00:34:15.408
I don't feel anything...

00:34:15.486 --> 00:34:17.681
not about my dead friends,

00:34:17.755 --> 00:34:19.416
not about Tom...

00:34:19.490 --> 00:34:21.685
you, my job.

00:34:21.759 --> 00:34:22.885
Maybe you're afraid

00:34:22.960 --> 00:34:25.588
if you let yourself
start to feel something,

00:34:25.663 --> 00:34:27.563
you might not be able to stop.

00:34:29.200 --> 00:34:32.636
You can't just shut off
your emotions, B'Elanna.

00:34:32.703 --> 00:34:34.068
Sooner or later...

00:34:34.138 --> 00:34:37.198
you're going to have
to let yourself grieve.

00:34:37.275 --> 00:34:39.209
Why?

00:34:39.277 --> 00:34:42.041
Just so I can go through it
all over again?

00:34:42.113 --> 00:34:43.978
What are you talking about?

00:34:47.585 --> 00:34:51.043
When I was six,
my father walked out on me.

00:34:51.122 --> 00:34:53.750
When I was 19,
I got kicked out of Starfleet.

00:34:53.825 --> 00:34:56.623
A few years later, I got
separated from the Maquis.

00:34:56.694 --> 00:34:58.559
And just when I
start to feel safe,

00:34:58.629 --> 00:35:00.790
you tell me that all
of our old friends

00:35:00.865 --> 00:35:03.732
have been slaughtered.

00:35:03.801 --> 00:35:07.794
The way I figure it, I've lost
every family I've ever had.

00:35:07.872 --> 00:35:10.568
B'Elanna...

00:35:10.641 --> 00:35:14.270
you have a new family now...
here on Voyager

00:35:14.345 --> 00:35:16.745
and you're not going to lose us.

00:35:16.814 --> 00:35:18.805
You're stuck with us.

00:35:18.883 --> 00:35:21.818
You can't promise me that.

00:35:21.886 --> 00:35:23.911
No, I suppose I can't.

00:35:24.055 --> 00:35:26.023
Losing people is inevitable,

00:35:26.090 --> 00:35:30.356
and sometimes it happens
sooner than we expect...

00:35:30.428 --> 00:35:33.420
but I can promise you
that the people on this ship

00:35:33.498 --> 00:35:35.932
aren't about to let you
stop living your life

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.934
or break your neck
on the holodeck.

00:35:38.035 --> 00:35:41.163
You're going to have to find
another way to deal with this.

00:35:45.109 --> 00:35:47.475
I don't know how.

00:35:48.946 --> 00:35:50.743
Then we'll figure it out...

00:35:50.815 --> 00:35:52.840
together.

00:35:55.019 --> 00:35:57.214
Commander Chakotay,
we're under attack.

00:35:57.288 --> 00:36:00.223
Report to the Bridge
immediately.

00:36:00.291 --> 00:36:01.451
You'd better go.

00:36:26.584 --> 00:36:28.575
Why are they suddenly
picking a fight?

00:36:28.653 --> 00:36:31.622
I believe they're attempting
to distract us, Commander,

00:36:31.689 --> 00:36:34.419
while they launch
their new shuttlecraft.

00:36:49.640 --> 00:36:51.608
The Malon vessel
is 42,000 kilometers

00:36:51.676 --> 00:36:53.143
from the probe and closing.

00:36:53.211 --> 00:36:54.542
We can still catch them.

00:36:54.612 --> 00:36:56.239
Bridge to Lieutenant Paris.

00:36:56.314 --> 00:36:57.303
Paris here.

00:36:57.381 --> 00:36:58.643
We've got to launch now

00:36:58.716 --> 00:37:01.048
if we're going
to get to the probe first.

00:37:01.118 --> 00:37:02.176
Are you ready?

00:37:02.253 --> 00:37:03.345
Yes, ma'am.

00:37:03.421 --> 00:37:05.252
I'll begin
the prelaunch sequence.

00:37:05.323 --> 00:37:07.314
What about
the microfracture problem?

00:37:07.391 --> 00:37:08.551
We're keeping an eye on it,

00:37:08.626 --> 00:37:10.253
but we sure could use
an extra hand.

00:37:10.328 --> 00:37:11.590
Chakotay's on his way.

00:37:24.408 --> 00:37:25.466
Chakotay...

00:37:25.543 --> 00:37:26.567
let me go.

00:37:26.644 --> 00:37:27.770
B'Elanna, I'm in a hurry.

00:37:27.845 --> 00:37:30.507
I am not out to get myself hurt
if that's what you're thinking.

00:37:30.581 --> 00:37:32.242
I just want to do my job.

00:37:32.316 --> 00:37:34.750
I thought you weren't interested
in your job anymore.

00:37:34.819 --> 00:37:39.188
If that hull breaches,
I should be there.

00:37:39.257 --> 00:37:41.191
I'm still the best engineer
we've got.

00:37:41.259 --> 00:37:42.658
Not lately.

00:37:42.727 --> 00:37:45.195
I can do this.

00:37:45.263 --> 00:37:47.322
I need to do this.

00:38:07.518 --> 00:38:08.883
40 seconds to launch.

00:38:08.986 --> 00:38:10.681
Powering impulse engines.

00:38:10.755 --> 00:38:13.724
Stand by to bring aft thrusters
on line.

00:38:15.826 --> 00:38:16.884
B'Elanna.

00:38:17.028 --> 00:38:19.622
I heard you might need some help

00:38:19.697 --> 00:38:21.289
keeping this thing
from falling apart.

00:38:22.833 --> 00:38:24.027
Welcome aboard.

00:38:25.670 --> 00:38:26.898
Vorik, you're in my seat.

00:38:26.971 --> 00:38:28.438
Excuse me, Lieutenant.

00:38:33.611 --> 00:38:34.805
20 seconds to launch.

00:38:34.879 --> 00:38:37.473
Get that hatch closed.

00:38:37.548 --> 00:38:39.311
Hatch sealed.

00:38:39.383 --> 00:38:40.850
Give me aft thrusters.

00:38:40.918 --> 00:38:43.148
Aft thrusters enabled.

00:38:43.220 --> 00:38:44.653
Ten seconds.

00:38:44.722 --> 00:38:45.848
All right.

00:38:45.923 --> 00:38:48.323
Let's see what this baby can do.

00:38:49.894 --> 00:38:50.826
Five...

00:38:50.895 --> 00:38:52.192
four...

00:38:52.263 --> 00:38:53.230
three...

00:38:53.297 --> 00:38:54.696
two...

00:38:54.765 --> 00:38:55.493
one.

00:39:06.510 --> 00:39:08.273
The Delta Flyer is away,
Captain.

00:39:08.346 --> 00:39:10.871
How long till they overtake
the Malon shuttle?

00:39:10.948 --> 00:39:14.111
At present velocity,
approximately three minutes.

00:39:21.959 --> 00:39:23.290
We're in.

00:39:23.361 --> 00:39:25.886
Structural integrity's
at 92 percent.

00:39:25.963 --> 00:39:29.899
There's the Malon shuttle...
200 kilometers off the port bow

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.468
and 3,000 kilometers
from the probe.

00:39:32.536 --> 00:39:33.730
We'll catch them.

00:39:33.804 --> 00:39:35.135
B'Elanna, how's the hull?

00:39:35.206 --> 00:39:38.801
Structural integrity's down
about 12 percent.

00:39:44.248 --> 00:39:46.341
They're launching
spatial charges.

00:39:46.417 --> 00:39:47.406
Shields holding.

00:39:47.485 --> 00:39:48.918
They want to play dirty.

00:39:48.986 --> 00:39:50.647
Let's show them what a little

00:39:50.721 --> 00:39:52.484
Borg-inspired weaponry
can do.

00:39:52.556 --> 00:39:54.387
Acknowledged.

00:39:54.458 --> 00:39:57.621
Loading photonic missiles.

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:01.895
We've lost power
to secondary systems.

00:40:01.966 --> 00:40:02.728
Fire.

00:40:05.803 --> 00:40:06.929
Three direct hits.

00:40:07.004 --> 00:40:08.596
They're losing attitude control.

00:40:08.672 --> 00:40:09.798
They're pulling up.

00:40:09.874 --> 00:40:11.273
Nice shooting, Seven.

00:40:12.710 --> 00:40:15.042
I'm taking us
down to the target.

00:40:15.112 --> 00:40:17.603
Harry, get ready
to grab the probe.

00:40:17.681 --> 00:40:19.740
Still out of transport range.

00:40:19.817 --> 00:40:22.285
We're losing integrity.
50 percent...

00:40:22.353 --> 00:40:23.650
forty...

00:40:23.721 --> 00:40:25.746
If you can hold us together
for another half a minute,

00:40:25.823 --> 00:40:27.313
we'll be within range
of the target.

00:40:27.391 --> 00:40:29.484
We still need
to survive the ascent.

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.494
One thing at a time.

00:40:31.562 --> 00:40:32.961
We're losing
structural integrity.

00:40:33.030 --> 00:40:34.292
It's down to 25 percent.

00:40:34.365 --> 00:40:35.627
Harry, prepare to lock on.

00:40:37.101 --> 00:40:40.468
We've got microfractures
forming... aft starboard hull

00:40:40.538 --> 00:40:41.630
zone two.

00:40:41.705 --> 00:40:42.967
I've got a lock.

00:40:43.107 --> 00:40:46.372
Beaming the probe
into the cargo hold.

00:40:46.444 --> 00:40:47.433
Got it.

00:40:47.511 --> 00:40:49.376
Initiating rapid ascent.

00:40:53.751 --> 00:40:55.514
Harry, I need
those secondary systems

00:40:55.586 --> 00:40:56.575
back on line.

00:40:56.654 --> 00:40:58.349
I can't. They're fried.

00:41:27.318 --> 00:41:29.149
Lieutenant, what are you doing?

00:41:29.220 --> 00:41:31.518
Patching a hole before it opens.

00:41:31.589 --> 00:41:33.147
That'll never hold.

00:41:33.224 --> 00:41:34.384
It'll hold a minute or two,

00:41:34.458 --> 00:41:36.085
and with any luck,
that's all we need.

00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:37.149
Seven, take over here.

00:41:47.071 --> 00:41:48.971
I need an EPS relay.

00:41:49.106 --> 00:41:51.939
Uh, there's one in the
transporter control circuitry.

00:41:57.548 --> 00:41:58.776
The panel is sealed.

00:41:58.849 --> 00:42:00.339
Good. Get away from it.

00:42:09.627 --> 00:42:11.458
I need a phaser.

00:42:39.924 --> 00:42:40.948
Watch out.

00:42:41.091 --> 00:42:44.151
I don't know
if this is going to work.

00:43:00.377 --> 00:43:02.072
Glad you decided to come along.

00:43:13.223 --> 00:43:14.690
The Delta Flyer has docked.

00:43:14.758 --> 00:43:16.191
And the Malon?

00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:18.194
They're a little preoccupied.

00:43:18.262 --> 00:43:21.322
Seems their shuttlecraft's
having a problem

00:43:21.398 --> 00:43:24.390
climbing out of the
gas giant's atmosphere.

00:43:24.468 --> 00:43:27.232
Get us out of here, Ensign...
warp 2.

00:43:27.304 --> 00:43:28.328
Aye, Captain.

00:43:40.050 --> 00:43:41.017
B'Elanna.

00:43:43.487 --> 00:43:45.921
I heard you did a hell of a job.

00:43:48.759 --> 00:43:50.249
So? How are you?

00:43:50.327 --> 00:43:54.388
You mean am I back
to my old charming self?

00:43:54.465 --> 00:43:56.296
I don't know.

00:43:57.835 --> 00:43:59.530
Give it time.

00:44:02.573 --> 00:44:05.133
Chakotay.

00:44:05.209 --> 00:44:08.804
What you did
down in the holodeck today...

00:44:08.879 --> 00:44:10.642
thanks.

00:44:12.650 --> 00:44:15.710
But if you ever do anything
like that again,

00:44:15.786 --> 00:44:17.310
I'll break your neck.

00:44:31.735 --> 00:44:33.293
Computer...

00:44:33.370 --> 00:44:37.170
one stack of banana pancakes
with maple syrup.
